okens": 2001, "total_tokens": 2001}}, "input": {"input": ["FITBIT PAY:FITBIT PAY is a mobile payment system that was launched in October 2018. It is designed to cater to active individuals and athletes, providing them with a convenient and secure way to make payments on the go. The system is available through select banks in Poland, allowing users to link their bank accounts to their Fitbit devices. This integration enables users to make contactless payments directly from their Fitbit smartwatches or fitness trackers, eliminating the need to carry cash or cards during workouts or daily activities. By focusing on the needs of active users, FITBIT PAY offers a seamless payment experience that aligns with the lifestyle of its target audience.", "SWATCHPAY:SwatchPay is a mobile payment system launched in December 2020, designed for use with Swatch watches", "XIAOMI PAY:Xiaomi Pay is a mobile payment system that was launched in October 2021. It is available in Poland through several banks, including Bank Pocztowy, SGB, and mBank. This service allows users to make payments using their mobile devices, providing a convenient and modern alternative to traditional payment methods. Xiaomi Pay's integration with these banks enables customers to easily manage their transactions and finances through their smartphones, enhancing the overall banking experience.", "BANK ZACHODNI WBK:Bank Zachodni WBK, which is now known as Santander Bank Polska, has played a significant role in the evolution of banking technology in Poland. The bank was a pioneer in the development of mobile banking and contributed to the establishment of the Polish Standard of Payments. In 2000, Bank Zachodni WBK made a notable advancement by becoming the first bank in Poland to launch a mobile website using the Wireless Application Protocol (WAP). This initiative marked a significant milestone in the Polish banking sector, showcasing the bank's commitment to innovation and its leadership in adopting new technologies to enhance customer experience. Through these efforts, Bank Zachodni WBK, now operating as Santander Bank Polska, has established itself as a forward-thinking institution in the financial industry.", "PEOPAY:", "IKO:", "BANK POCZTOWY:Bank Pocztowy is a financial institution based in Poland, known for its comprehensive range of mobile banking and payment services. The bank provides its customers with various secure mobile banking login methods, including PIN, fingerprint, and face scan, ensuring a high level of security and convenience for its users. \n\nIn the realm of mobile payments, Bank Pocztowy offers an extensive array of options to cater to the diverse needs of its clientele. These include popular systems such as BLIK, Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, and Xiaomi Pay. Notably, the bank has been offering BLIK services since 2020, highlighting its commitment to integrating modern payment solutions into its offerings. \n\nDespite being part of a group characterized by lower than average mobile banking indicators, Bank Pocztowy stands out with a significant percentage of 'mobile only' users, indicating a strong adoption of mobile banking among its customer base. This suggests that while the overall mobile banking metrics may be lower, the bank has successfully cultivated a dedicated segment of users who rely exclusively on mobile platforms for their banking needs.\n\nOverall, Bank Pocztowy is a key player in the Polish banking sector, particularly in the context of mobile banking and payment systems, continually enhancing its services to meet the evolving demands of its customers.", "SGB:SGB is a cooperative banking group based in Poland, recognized for its diverse range of mobile banking services and security features. As a financial institution, SGB has been proactive in integrating modern technology into its banking solutions, offering customers convenient and secure access to their accounts. Among the services provided by SGB is the SGB Mobile application, which enhances user experience by allowing mobile banking login methods such as PIN and fingerprint authentication. This focus on mobile banking security underscores SGB's commitment to safeguarding customer information and ensuring secure transactions.\n\nIn addition to these features, SGB has embraced innovative payment solutions by incorporating Xiaomi Pay into its offerings, providing customers with more flexibility and convenience in managing their finances. Since 2021, SGB has also been offering BLIK services, a popular mobile payment system in Poland, further expanding its digital banking capabilities and aligning with the evolving needs of its clientele.\n\nDespite its advancements in mobile banking and payment services, SGB was excluded from a particular analysis due to missing data. This exclusion highlights a potential area for improvement in data management and availability, which could enhance the bank's participation in future analyses and studies.\n\nOverall, SGB stands out as a forward-thinking cooperative banking group in Poland, dedicated to providing secure, innovative, and user-friendly banking solutions to its customers.", "EUROPEAN CENTRAL BANK:The European Central Bank defines mobile payments as payments where a mobile device is used at least to initiate a payment order and potentially to transfer funds", "HARASIM:HARASIM is a researcher known for their contributions to the field of mobile payments and consumer payment preferences. They have provided a detailed definition of mobile payments, emphasizing the role of mobile devices and technology in facilitating communication and data transmission during transactions. HARASIM's work highlights the technological aspects of mobile payments, underscoring how these innovations are integral to modern financial transactions.\n\nIn addition to defining mobile payments, HARASIM has conducted studies on consumer preferences for cashless payments. Their research explores how consumers are increasingly favoring cashless options, driven by the convenience and efficiency offered by mobile payment technologies. Through their studies, HARASIM has contributed valuable insights into the evolving landscape of consumer payment preferences, shedding light on the factors that influence the adoption of cashless payment methods.\n\nOverall, HARASIM's work provides a comprehensive understanding of mobile payments and consumer behavior in the context of cashless transactions, making significant contributions to the field of financial technology research.", "KISIEL:KISIEL is an author who has made significant contributions to the understanding of internet banking in Poland. Through extensive characterization, KISIEL has provided valuable insights into the dynamics and intricacies of online financial transactions within the Polish banking sector. In addition to this, KISIEL has also defined mobile payments, describing them as the process of transferring funds using a mobile phone to initiate, confirm, and finalize transactions. This definition highlights the role of mobile technology in modern financial operations, emphasizing the convenience and efficiency it brings to the process of managing and executing financial transactions. Through these contributions, KISIEL has played a pivotal role in elucidating the evolving landscape of digital banking and payments, offering a comprehensive perspective on how technology is reshaping financial services in Poland.", "KORENIK:KORENIK is an accomplished author and researcher with a focus on the financial sector, particularly in Poland. KORENIK has extensively characterized internet banking in Poland, providing valuable insights into its development, challenges, and impact on the financial landscape. In addition to this, KORENIK has explored the broader role of banks in supporting innovation within a knowledge-based economy. Through their research, KORENIK discusses how banks can act as catalysts for innovation, facilitating the growth and development of new ideas and technologies. By examining the intersection of banking and innovation, KORENIK contributes to a deeper understanding of how financial institutions can drive economic progress in a rapidly evolving digital world.", "KOŹLIŃSKI:An author who has extensively characterized internet banking in Poland", "POLASIK:POLASIK is an author and researcher who has made significant contributions to the understanding of internet and mobile banking, particularly in the context of Poland. Through extensive characterization, POLASIK has provided valuable insights into the landscape of internet banking within the country, highlighting its development and the various factors influencing its adoption and usage.\n\nIn addition to internet banking, POLASIK has also focused on the realm of mobile banking applications. He has provided commentary on the financial aspects of these applications, specifically addressing the costs associated with their implementation and ongoing maintenance. This analysis is crucial for financial institutions and developers as they navigate the economic challenges of offering mobile banking services.\n\nFurthermore, POLASIK, in collaboration with Maciejewski, has explored the intricate nature of mobile payments. They have emphasized the complexity involved in mobile payments, which arises from the integration of diverse communication technologies within mobile devices. This complexity presents both challenges and opportunities for the development and enhancement of mobile payment systems.\n\nOverall, POLASIK's work provides a comprehensive view of the evolving banking technologies in Poland, offering insights into both the technical and economic dimensions of internet and mobile banking. His research is instrumental for stakeholders in the financial sector who are looking to understand and leverage these technologies effectively.", "ŚWIECKA:ŚWIECKA is a distinguished author and researcher with a focus on financial systems and consumer behavior in Poland. She has made significant contributions to the understanding of internet banking, providing extensive characterizations of its development and impact within the country. Her research delves into consumer payment preferences, offering insights into how individuals choose between various payment methods in an increasingly digital economy.\n\nIn 2016, Świecka brought attention to the concerning issue of the low level of economic knowledge among children and youth in Poland. Her work in this area underscores the importance of financial education and literacy, advocating for improved educational strategies to better prepare younger generations for financial decision-making.\n\nAdditionally, Świecka has defined mobile payments as a form of cashless payment that facilitates both financial and non-financial transactions through the use of mobile devices. Her definition highlights the versatility and growing importance of mobile technology in modern financial transactions, reflecting her broader interest in the evolution of payment systems.\n\nThrough her research and publications, Świecka has contributed valuable knowledge to the fields of internet banking, consumer payment preferences, and financial literacy, making her a prominent figure in the study of financial behaviors and systems in Poland.", "GOSPODAROWICZ:"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_deb2a852a7ee03836e5a68bf846baa5d55a6ed6365ad1936e3f0450ae0009003_v2"}